# title: Quanto call
# category: Vanillas and digitals
# underlyings: 1
# quanto: USD
# source: Reiner, Quanto Mechanics, Risk 5(3), 1992
# source: Hull, Options, Futures, and Other Derivatives, 11th ed., Pearson, ch. 30 (quantos)
# summary: A call on a stock listed in another currency, its gain paid in dollars at an exchange rate fixed today: the investor takes the stock's risk, not the currency's.
# param: strike = 1.0 | percent | Strike, % of the initial level
# param: fixed_rate = 1.0 | number | Dollars paid per unit of the stock's currency
#
# Simulated in dollars: the stock drifts at its own currency's rate, less its
# dividend, less rho sigma_S sigma_X (the quanto adjustment), X its currency
# in dollars.

2027-01-04
    strike = 1.0
    fixed_rate = 1.0
    s0 = spot()

2028-01-04
    pays fixed_rate * max(spot() - strike * s0, 0)
